    "result_text": "All 267 tests pass, including the new cp07 test. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented owner initials by following the existing `displayName` pattern (added in cp06):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `initials` field to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the property.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct expression mapping that computes initials from the entity:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\" + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\")\")\n   ```\n   This upper-cases the first letters of the first and last name, dot-separates them, and adds a trailing dot (e.g. `John` + `Sur\u2026` \u2192 `J.S.`).\n\nBecause the mapping lives in `toOwnerDto`, initials are populated on every owner response (create, get, list), and the cp07 test \u2014 which creates an owner then GETs it to assert `$.initials == \"J.S.\"` \u2014 passes. The full suite (267 tests) is green.",
